WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.501
-Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy-

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:04.904
and Grammy Award-winning
comedian you know from her work

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:08.274
in "Girls Trip," "The Last OG,"
and "The Afterparty."

00:00:08.274 --> 00:00:12.045
Her children's book,
"Layla, The Last Black Unicorn,"

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:14.314
hits shelves May 10th,
and you can see her

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:15.714
in the new Nicolas Cage film

00:00:15.714 --> 00:00:17.783
"The Unbearable Weight
of Massive Talent"

00:00:17.783 --> 00:00:19.685
in theaters tomorrow.
Let's take a look.

00:00:19.685 --> 00:00:21.420
-Wait, wait, wait, wait,
wait, wait, wait.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:23.289
Why is Nic Cage on this plane?

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:25.024
You know what?
We're pulling out.

00:00:25.024 --> 00:00:26.792
-I don't like this.
Get out of there.

00:00:26.792 --> 00:00:28.061
-No.
-What do you mean "no"?

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:29.129
No, no, no.
What are you doing?

00:00:29.129 --> 00:00:30.897
Vivian, what are you doing?

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:32.665
-Thank you.

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:33.933
-This is our shot.

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:35.534
-No, get out!

00:00:35.534 --> 00:00:37.736
Vivian, get the f--
-Nicolas Cage!

00:00:37.736 --> 00:00:40.907
Oh, my God!
You're so awesome.

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:43.243
I love you!
-Oh, thank you.

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:46.245
-Me and my nephew, Raymond,
just watched "Croods 2."

00:00:46.245 --> 00:00:49.315
Dude cracked us up.

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:50.817
Can I take a selfie?
-Sure.

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:52.485
No, I like that movie, too.

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:54.119
-You did so good
in that movie, man.

00:00:54.119 --> 00:00:56.289
-I made that movie
with Emma Stone.

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:58.725
-Please welcome
back to the show

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:00.359
our friend Tiffany Haddish!

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:02.361
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:02.361 --> 00:01:12.371 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:12.371 --> 00:01:19.779 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:21.780
-Hey!
-Oh, my goodness!

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:24.450
I'm so glad you're back.
-I'm so glad to be back.

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:26.886
Is that drummer married?
-That drummer? I don't know.

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:28.921
Aric, are you married?
-I'm about to be.

00:01:28.921 --> 00:01:30.122
-Oh, about to be.
[ Audience groans ]

00:01:30.122 --> 00:01:32.158
I don't know. He left
a window open for you.

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:34.394
-I know, "about to," right?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:37.230
I'm cool on "about to."
I need to know, you available?

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.597
[ Laughter ]
-Because you are.

00:01:38.597 --> 00:01:39.632
You're dating again.

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:41.033
-Yes, I'm back out
in the streets.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:43.269
-How's it going?
-Um, you know, it's --

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:45.205
it's interesting.
It's an adventure.

00:01:45.205 --> 00:01:46.271
-Yeah.

00:01:46.271 --> 00:01:47.540
-You know, I'm all about
adventure.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.075
-Yeah.
-I'm back on the dating apps.

00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:52.545
You know, I put all my
requirements in my profile.

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:54.313
-Okay.
What are the big ones?

00:01:54.313 --> 00:01:56.716
-Good credit score, because I
need to know you responsible.

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:58.551
-Yeah.
-Okay.

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:00.352
You need to have good hygiene.
-All right.

00:02:00.352 --> 00:02:01.487
-That's really important to me.

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:03.889
I can't stand bad breath
and funky armpits.

00:02:03.889 --> 00:02:06.192
-Yeah.
-What else? What else?

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:09.429
Oh, you need to have --
Okay, so, you know,

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:11.564
I've been attracted to a lot of
hip-hop kind of guys.

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:12.631
-Yeah.

00:02:12.631 --> 00:02:14.567
-And I don't mind men
wearing jewelry.

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:17.003
But if you own
a bunch of diamonds

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:19.371
but you don't own no land?
-Yeah.

00:02:19.371 --> 00:02:21.440
-That's a problem for me.
-So you want land.

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:23.609
You would prefer land
and then diamonds.

00:02:23.609 --> 00:02:24.777
-Land then diamonds.

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:26.112
Because where do
the diamonds come from?

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:27.780
The land.
-Yes.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:31.283
-So own the land,
then get the diamonds.

00:02:31.283 --> 00:02:32.952
Like, I got diamonds.
-Yeah.

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:34.253
-I do.
'Cause I got land.

00:02:34.253 --> 00:02:36.255
-Oh, interesting.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:36.255 --> 00:02:39.592
I think that is
very interesting.

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:41.861
People must be so excited
to go on a date with you,

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:45.731
but then also maybe
a little intimidated.

00:02:45.731 --> 00:02:46.933
-I don't know
if they're intimi--

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:49.335
I think all men are scary.
-Yeah.

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:50.803
-I think y'all all scared.

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:52.638
I can feel
your intimidation right now.

00:02:52.638 --> 00:02:54.240
-That I'm currently
intimidated by you?

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.675
-Just a little bit.
I see your forehead

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:58.043
turning a little bit red.
-Well...

00:02:58.043 --> 00:02:59.979
I'm gonna come little closer
to show you.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:03.115
[ Both laugh ]
-See? Yeah!

00:03:03.115 --> 00:03:06.352
-Yeah?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:08.387
I'll tell you what I'm
intimidated about, for real.

00:03:08.387 --> 00:03:09.889
Here's what
I'm intimidated about.

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:11.224
-What?
-Your kids book.

00:03:11.224 --> 00:03:12.225
-Why?

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:13.425
-'Cause I got a kids book
right now.

00:03:13.425 --> 00:03:14.494
-Oh, yeah,
you do got a kids book.

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:16.963
-And I am holding on by a thread

00:03:16.963 --> 00:03:19.131
to the "New York Times"
bestseller top 10.

00:03:19.131 --> 00:03:20.766
I mean,
I'm on a thread right now.

00:03:20.766 --> 00:03:22.635
-What number are you now?
-Nine.

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:25.137
-Oh, okay.
Well, get ready to be 13.

00:03:25.137 --> 00:03:27.039
-[ Laughing ] 13?
So this is yours.

00:03:27.039 --> 00:03:28.141
-Yes, yes.
-All right.

00:03:28.141 --> 00:03:29.875
And this is very exciting.
-Yes.

00:03:29.875 --> 00:03:32.778
It's based off
of a portion of my childhood.

00:03:32.778 --> 00:03:35.114
-Uh-huh.
-I had to go to this new school,

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:37.083
and I was feeling
really uncomfortable there

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:38.351
'cause I didn't think
I would fit in.

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:40.820
And I didn't, at first,
but I figured my way out

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:43.889
and figured out how to use
my special gifts

00:03:43.889 --> 00:03:45.792
as a way to make friends.

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:48.127
So that's what this is about.
-Did you enjoy it?

00:03:48.127 --> 00:03:49.795
Did you enjoy the process
of writing a kids book?

00:03:49.795 --> 00:03:50.963
-I did enjoy the process.

00:03:50.963 --> 00:03:52.498
Did you enjoy it?
-I did.

00:03:52.498 --> 00:03:53.832
-What did you like
most about it?

00:03:53.832 --> 00:03:56.135
-I liked that someone else
did the drawings.

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:58.537
[ Laughter ]

00:03:58.537 --> 00:04:00.840
-You should've seen my sketches.
It was all stick figures.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.942
-Yeah.
Did you actually do it, though?

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:04.243
Did you say to your artist,
like,

00:04:04.243 --> 00:04:05.277
"I've done some
stick-figure work for you"?

00:04:05.277 --> 00:04:07.312
-Yeah, I'm like,
"Here go some ideas."

00:04:07.312 --> 00:04:09.415
-Uh-huh.
-And then I just started

00:04:09.415 --> 00:04:12.084
cutting and pasting
other unicorn things

00:04:12.084 --> 00:04:14.553
I liked onto it,
so I made, like, a collage.

00:04:14.553 --> 00:04:16.856
-You did a lot more than I did.
That's very impressive.

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:18.891
-Well, 'cause I'm very specific
about what I do.

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:20.593
That's how you get bestseller
all the time.

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:25.131
-Interesting.
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:04:25.131 --> 00:04:28.901
Well, I'm here to tell you that
if you mail it in, effort-wise,

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:32.004
you get that number nine
as the sweet spot.

00:04:32.004 --> 00:04:34.607
You can settle right in
to number nine.

00:04:34.607 --> 00:04:37.109
-Everybody, make sure you get
Seth's book now,

00:04:37.109 --> 00:04:40.113
'cause when mine comes out
May 10th, it's a wrap for him.

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:42.014
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.014 --> 00:04:43.683
-I can't wait.
On May 10th --

00:04:43.683 --> 00:04:47.587
On May 10th, you're gonna see my
book in all the half-off bins.

00:04:47.587 --> 00:04:49.355
"We needed shelf space
for Tiffany."

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:51.290
-Have you gone to read
to the kids yet?

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:54.193
-I'm doing a reading,
'cause when it first came out,

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:56.995
it was still a little bit like,
we're not doing in-person stuff,

00:04:56.995 --> 00:04:58.497
but I'm doing one in two weeks.
I'm really excited.

00:04:58.497 --> 00:04:59.766
-Oh, that's awesome.

00:04:59.766 --> 00:05:02.268
I've already been reading mine
in Zooms.

00:05:02.268 --> 00:05:03.369
-You're doing Zooms?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.369 --> 00:05:05.505
-I've been to hospitals
through Zoom.

00:05:05.505 --> 00:05:07.273
-Well, that's wonderful
that you're doing that.

00:05:07.273 --> 00:05:08.908
-Yeah, it's called early
advertisement.

00:05:08.908 --> 00:05:11.010
-Oh, interesting.
-Yeah, that's part of why

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:12.712
I did the children's book,
'cause, see, I want to reach

00:05:12.712 --> 00:05:15.047
all demographics,
and I know children love me.

00:05:15.047 --> 00:05:16.415
-Uh-huh.
-I don't know if you ever had

00:05:16.415 --> 00:05:19.318
a 4-year-old tell you
you a big deal, but I have.

00:05:19.318 --> 00:05:21.554
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:23.189
When that 4-year-old told me
I was a big deal,

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:24.390
I said, "You know what?

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:26.191
I got to do something
for that 4-year-old."

00:05:26.191 --> 00:05:27.859
-Yes.
-So I went ahead

00:05:27.859 --> 00:05:30.362
and made this book
for ages 3 to 8.

00:05:30.362 --> 00:05:31.798
That's a whole new demographic.

00:05:31.798 --> 00:05:34.700
By the time they old enough
to spend they own money, bam!

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:36.369
They my customers!
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.369 --> 00:05:40.339
-No, because I should say,
I love when an old person

00:05:40.339 --> 00:05:42.107
comes up and tells me,
"I love your work."

00:05:42.107 --> 00:05:43.276
I love that a great deal.

00:05:43.276 --> 00:05:45.278
But I know they're not
gonna be around forever.

00:05:45.278 --> 00:05:49.482
-Yeah, but they gonna leave
their money to somebody,

00:05:49.482 --> 00:05:53.886
and you want the somebody
to spend it on you.

00:05:53.886 --> 00:05:55.687
I believe children
are my future.

00:05:55.687 --> 00:05:57.323
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:57.323 --> 00:05:58.324
Hello.

00:05:58.324 --> 00:06:00.493
-So I'm excited about your book.

00:06:00.493 --> 00:06:01.861
I'm so excited for this movie.

00:06:01.861 --> 00:06:03.729
When I first heard about
this movie, I thought,

00:06:03.729 --> 00:06:05.331
"This can't possibly be real."

00:06:05.331 --> 00:06:08.167
Nic Cage is playing Nic Cage.

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:11.904
And he gets paid
a million dollars to go to,

00:06:11.904 --> 00:06:13.839
basically, a rich
person's...birthday party?

00:06:13.839 --> 00:06:16.809
-Yes, which I wish would happen
for me in real life.

00:06:16.809 --> 00:06:18.544
I mean, I go to birthday parties
all the time.

00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:20.646
Nobody ever gives me nothing.

00:06:20.646 --> 00:06:22.047
[ Laughter ]

00:06:22.047 --> 00:06:24.350
But they so happy I'm there,
and they take a lot of pictures.

00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:27.085
Right?
So when I first read the script,

00:06:27.085 --> 00:06:28.554
I was like,
"Oh, y'all finna get, like,

00:06:28.554 --> 00:06:30.956
a Nic Cage impersonator, right?
'Cause this ain't really --"

00:06:30.956 --> 00:06:32.458
And they was like,
"No, we got Nicolas Cage."

00:06:32.458 --> 00:06:34.961
I was like, "For real?"
[ Laughter ]

00:06:34.961 --> 00:06:38.598
"He gonna do this for real?
Is this his real-life story?"

00:06:38.598 --> 00:06:39.865
[ Laughter ]

00:06:39.865 --> 00:06:41.868
And they said,
"No, it's just a way to, like,

00:06:41.868 --> 00:06:44.603
show his works
and for him to poke fun."

00:06:44.603 --> 00:06:47.907
And I was thinking to myself,
"Is he a comedic actor at all?"

00:06:47.907 --> 00:06:51.210
But then I realized, he's a
freakin' phenomenal actor.

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:52.745
-He is.
-So when you're a great actor,

00:06:52.745 --> 00:06:55.014
you can do anything, right?
-Yeah.

00:06:55.014 --> 00:06:57.516
-So I was super excited
to meet him.

00:06:57.516 --> 00:06:59.118
And that's part of why
I wanted to do the movie,

00:06:59.118 --> 00:07:00.986
'cause I wanted to tell him
a story.

00:07:00.986 --> 00:07:02.187
And then -- that's it.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:02.187 --> 00:07:03.455
I just wanted to tell him
one story

00:07:03.455 --> 00:07:05.124
and make that money
at the same time.

00:07:05.124 --> 00:07:06.825
-Yeah, yeah, that's a --

00:07:06.825 --> 00:07:08.894
If you can tell a story
and get paid --

00:07:08.894 --> 00:07:10.929
What was the story
you had to tell Nic Cage?

00:07:10.929 --> 00:07:13.699
-Okay, so -- I mean,
I told it to a few reporters.

00:07:13.699 --> 00:07:15.634
It ended up being clickbait.

00:07:15.634 --> 00:07:18.804
But what had happened was,
when I was 17,

00:07:18.804 --> 00:07:21.040
I had went on a date
to the movies, right?

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:25.478
And it was my first time
experiencing a climax

00:07:25.478 --> 00:07:28.948
in a movie theater.
-Wait. So not a film climax?

00:07:28.948 --> 00:07:31.583
-Oh, no, no, a personal --
you know, um...

00:07:31.583 --> 00:07:32.852
[ Laughter ]
-Okay.

00:07:32.852 --> 00:07:34.120
-Ladies, you know
what I'm talking about.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:35.554
Ooh!
[ Laughter ]

00:07:35.554 --> 00:07:37.356
Whoa!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:37.356 --> 00:07:40.092
"Yaah!
What's happening to me?!"

00:07:40.092 --> 00:07:42.928
-So this was happening --
So this was happening --

00:07:42.928 --> 00:07:44.496
-So what had happened was,

00:07:44.496 --> 00:07:46.933
it was just me and this guy
in the theater, right?

00:07:46.933 --> 00:07:49.368
We had went to the really
late show of "Face/Off,"

00:07:49.368 --> 00:07:51.737
which is my favorite movie.
-Yeah, okay.

00:07:51.737 --> 00:07:54.106
-So we went to the late showing
of "Face/Off," and then,

00:07:54.106 --> 00:07:56.108
you know, you be in there
making out and stuff.

00:07:56.108 --> 00:07:58.511
Yeah, yeah.
-Yeah, of course.

00:07:58.511 --> 00:08:00.679
And then, you know, he was,
like, moving his hands around

00:08:00.679 --> 00:08:03.015
and stuff, and I was like,
"Whoo!"

00:08:03.015 --> 00:08:05.685
and when I "Whoo!",
when I opened my eyes,

00:08:05.685 --> 00:08:08.487
Nicolas Cage eyes
was looking into my eyes.

00:08:08.487 --> 00:08:12.825
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:08:12.825 --> 00:08:14.660
And that's kind of the vision.

00:08:14.660 --> 00:08:16.094
That's what I seen
most of the time.

00:08:16.094 --> 00:08:18.363
That's my first experience
with --

00:08:18.363 --> 00:08:21.767
-So now every time...?
-No, not every time, no, no.

00:08:21.767 --> 00:08:24.369
Just when I close my eyes.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:24.369 --> 00:08:25.738
But that's
why I keep my eyes open.

00:08:25.738 --> 00:08:28.874
So when I meet Nicolas Cage,
you know, I get there

00:08:28.874 --> 00:08:30.542
first day of work,
and I'm thinking, like,

00:08:30.542 --> 00:08:32.577
"I'm gonna get to talk to him
for 30 minutes or so,

00:08:32.577 --> 00:08:34.447
and then I could tell him this,
and then get on --"

00:08:34.447 --> 00:08:37.249
But that's not how it went down.
It was like, straight to work.

00:08:37.249 --> 00:08:39.351
Bam!
We rehearse, and now we on.

00:08:39.351 --> 00:08:40.819
And I'm looking at him
in his eyes

00:08:40.819 --> 00:08:43.422
like I'm looking at you
in your eyes.

00:08:43.422 --> 00:08:47.192
And the 17-year-old me is like,
"Tell him, tell him!"

00:08:47.192 --> 00:08:49.094
And I'm like,
"No, shut up, bitch!

00:08:49.094 --> 00:08:50.429
You can't tell him now!

00:08:50.429 --> 00:08:52.197
It's inappropriate!
We at work!"

00:08:52.197 --> 00:08:53.932
"No, you got to tell him!"

00:08:53.932 --> 00:08:57.369
And then I couldn't do my lines.
It was bad.

00:08:57.369 --> 00:08:59.972
It was very bad.
I could not perform.

00:08:59.972 --> 00:09:03.041
And then, finally, after about
three hours of being horrible,

00:09:03.041 --> 00:09:05.477
I was like, "Look, I have
to tell you this story,

00:09:05.477 --> 00:09:07.779
or I'm not gonna be able to --
y'all gonna fire me."

00:09:07.779 --> 00:09:10.182
And I said, "It's a very
inappropriate story,

00:09:10.182 --> 00:09:11.316
but please let me tell you."

00:09:11.316 --> 00:09:15.121
And I told him,
and he laughed so hard.

00:09:15.121 --> 00:09:18.157
And then he told me a story
about how his first wife

00:09:18.157 --> 00:09:20.726
saw him in a movie and said,
"That's gonna be my husband,"

00:09:20.726 --> 00:09:22.394
and he ended up marrying her.
And I said,

00:09:22.394 --> 00:09:23.728
"Well, I'm gonna let you know
right now,

00:09:23.728 --> 00:09:25.931
you won't be fiddling
any of these beans over here."

00:09:25.931 --> 00:09:28.834
[ Laughter ]
"Okay?"

00:09:28.834 --> 00:09:30.269
And we been good friends
ever since.

00:09:30.269 --> 00:09:33.539
-That's fantastic.
I think that sometimes,

00:09:33.539 --> 00:09:35.608
you're so nervous
when you meet a person

00:09:35.608 --> 00:09:37.109
that you've looked up to
for so long,

00:09:37.109 --> 00:09:38.944
and you're so worried you're
going to tell them something

00:09:38.944 --> 00:09:40.579
they've heard a million times.
-Right.

00:09:40.579 --> 00:09:43.315
He never heard that before.
-Yeah, I was gonna wager, yeah.

00:09:43.315 --> 00:09:45.418
That was a first time
that he's ever heard that.

00:09:45.418 --> 00:09:47.753
-But then, after that,
my acting was excellent.

00:09:47.753 --> 00:09:49.154
[ Laughter ]
It was great.

00:09:49.154 --> 00:09:50.622
-Your acting
is always excellent.

00:09:50.622 --> 00:09:52.424
And let me tell you,
it is always such a joy

00:09:52.424 --> 00:09:53.625
to have you here.
Thank you so much.

00:09:53.625 --> 00:09:54.994
-It's always a joy to be here
with you, man.

00:09:54.994 --> 00:09:58.263
-It was such a delight.
Guys, that's Tiffany Haddish.

00:09:58.263 --> 00:09:59.965
"The Unbearable Weight
of Massive Talent"

00:09:59.965 --> 00:10:01.600
opens in theaters tomorrow.

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:05.571
And "Layla, The Last Black
Unicorn" is available May 10th.

00:10:05.571 --> 00:10:07.206
I'm so sorry.
Oh, my God. Is that my book?

00:10:07.206 --> 00:10:09.207
I'm so sorry.
-That's your book.

00:10:09.207 --> 00:10:11.911
-We'll be right back
with Chloe Sevigny.

